{
  "_id": "259Ey7LXgqL7ZDGJ8XK1vBJmZrh",
  "_type": "Doc",
  "_index": "a0",
  "title": "Configuration",
  "navigationTitle": "",
  "body": [
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "All configuration can be managed from the `cms.ts` file. This file is created in the project root (or your `src` folder if it exists) during `alinea init`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "CodeBlock",
      "_id": "2a4tC7lBmNMZUuJDec7zsG4st62",
      "code": "import {createCMS} from 'alinea/next'\n\nexport const cms = createCMS({\n  schema: {...},\n  workspaces: {...},\n  baseUrl: {\n    development: 'http://localhost:3000',\n    production: 'https://example.com'\n  },\n  handlerUrl: '/api/cms',\n  adminPath: '/admin',\n  enableDrafts: true,\n  preview: true\n})",
      "fileName": "cms.ts",
      "language": "tsx",
      "compact": false
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`schema`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "schema"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Describe the structure of your content using a "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "collection of Types",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "2YkhKab77FPvVbFuEKDFvTCeQqA",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "267KTV8uPHIdZgFUQvJf06sfm4h"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": ". Required."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`workspaces`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "workspaces"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Content can be bundled in separate "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Workspaces",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "2YkhLyWRcJ1TaBwxb1l8MIeWbGP",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "259EzPfnSUaKOrNL1S2bpIpMdKl"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": ". Defining at least one is required."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`baseUrl`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "baseurl"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The URL of the website where Alinea is used, either a single string or one per environment (`development` and `production`, picked by `NODE_ENV`). A value without a protocol gets `https://`. The production URL is required for a deployed site: the handler URL is resolved against it."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`handlerUrl`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "handlerurl"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The URL of the API route that serves the dashboard's requests, the route that exports `createHandler` from `alinea/next`. Required. `alinea init` sets it to `/api/cms` and creates the route in `app/(alinea)/api/cms/route.ts`. A relative URL is resolved against `baseUrl`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`adminPath`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "adminpath"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The path where the dashboard is served on your site, defaults to `/admin`. During development `withAlinea` forwards this path to the local dashboard of `alinea dev`, in production `alinea build` writes the dashboard to `public/admin.html` (named after the path) and `withAlinea` serves it from there. It can't be the root path `/`. This replaces the `dashboardFile` option of Alinea 1.x, which is deprecated."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`enableDrafts`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "enabledrafts"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Allows content editors to save and preview unpublished changes before publishing. "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`preview`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "preview"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Set to `true` to display an iframe with "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "live previews",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3JjypBvxQ7B90PqTq2hAlkJYWhH",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "2YlBsRF2vZwxcS27oOSJYmQM37q"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": " on the side of the editor."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`roles`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "roles"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Custom roles with permission policies, see "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Roles and permissions",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "3JjypA5bA8uqLK8XSUyeAoFSIOr",
              "_link": "entry",
              "_entry": "3AhqfX37Pijf2zOEwYVVU4NmdHG"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": ". An `admin` role is always available."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`syncInterval`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "syncinterval"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Content is refreshed when the site notices the repository changed. As a fallback the site also syncs at most once per interval, in seconds, defaults to 60. `0` syncs on every request."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`maxUploadSize`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "maxuploadsize"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The maximum size of an uploaded file, in bytes. Larger uploads are refused."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`publicDir`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "publicdir"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The folder your site serves static files from, defaults to `public`. Media stored inside it get public URLs."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "`tracer`"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "tracer"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "An optional function to instrument Alinea operations, for example with OpenTelemetry spans. It is called as `tracer(name, run)` and must return the result of `run()`."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Good to know"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "good-to-know"
    },
    {
      "_type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Dealing with errors"
        }
      ],
      "_anchor": "dealing-with-errors"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "Your config file is read and executed during the `alinea dev` and `alinea build` "
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "CLI",
          "marks": [
            {
              "_type": "link",
              "_id": "2bRPphjzKp0th73W5AIX4MbwCAC",
              "_entry": "m5KGP-I5smg2S8o4A-j15",
              "_link": "entry"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": " commands. If anything goes wrong, you might see an error such as:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "CodeBlock",
      "_id": "2bRPtrWBR0pa60dm18O0y8DW2u8",
      "code": "Error: Fail\n    at file:///home/alineacms/alinea/node_modules/@alinea/generated/config.js?1706175675574:419:7\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:194:25)",
      "fileName": "",
      "language": "shellscript"
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "To debug these situations Alinea compiles your config file with an included source map. To enable node to read the source map and report correct positions you can enable the Node.js `--enable-source-maps` flag. You can add it to the scripts in package.json:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "CodeBlock",
      "_id": "2bRQUBTqZ510BRTvtbDs333cnoR",
      "code": "{\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"dev\": \"NODE_OPTIONS=--enable-source-maps alinea dev -- next dev\",\n    \"build\": \"NODE_OPTIONS=--enable-source-maps alinea build -- next build\"\n  }\n}",
      "fileName": "",
      "language": "json"
    },
    {
      "_type": "NoticeBlock",
      "_id": "2bRQZBPfwzPF6lNUtjW0wVPFY06",
      "level": "info",
      "body": [
        {
          "_type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "_type": "text",
              "text": "If you're developing on Windows you can use "
            },
            {
              "_type": "text",
              "text": "cross-env",
              "marks": [
                {
                  "_type": "link",
                  "_id": "3JjypE032ZsmdNcMUIyalgHmMMT",
                  "_link": "url",
                  "href": "https://www.npmjs.com/package/cross-env"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_type": "text",
              "text": " to achieve the same."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "paragraph",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "content": [
        {
          "_type": "text",
          "text": "The error will now point to the right file:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "CodeBlock",
      "_id": "2bRR5xvNhvfy0EaJAgL0owbuNYV",
      "code": "Error: Fail\n    at <anonymous> (/home/alinea/apps/dev/cms.ts:278:7)\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:194:25)",
      "fileName": "",
      "language": "shellscript"
    }
  ],
